	<logo>https://static.globalissues.org/i/globalissues/logo-feed.jpg</logo><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/03/44251</id><title>Uganda’s UN-supported wildlife forensics lab turns ivory seizures into convictions</title><updated>2026-10-03T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/03/44251" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/28-09-2026_Adobe_Elephant.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/28-09-2026_Adobe_Elephant.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/28-09-2026_Adobe_Elephant.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/09/28-09-2026_Adobe_Elephant.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The package originated in Entebbe, Uganda, bound for Cairo, containing 10 kilograms of thumb-sized pieces that could have been either bone or elephant ivory.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/03/44251&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Uganda’s UN-supported wildlife forensics lab turns ivory seizures into convictions”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44242</id><title>Renewables, Farmer Aggregation Offer Solutions to Africa’s Post-Harvest Losses</title><updated>2026-10-02T08:43:46-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44242" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/06/Winner.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/06/Winner.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/06/Winner-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/06/Winner.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
KIGALI, October 2 (IPS)  - Post-harvest losses, particularly in rural areas, threaten the gains Africa is making in agricultural production and export capacity.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44242&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Renewables, Farmer Aggregation Offer Solutions to Africa’s Post-Harvest Losses”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44241</id><title>For Pakistan Rising Fistula Cases Make SDG 3 Goal Elusive</title><updated>2026-10-02T08:10:37-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44241" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/main-fistula-scaled-e1790927431938.png" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/main-fistula-scaled-e1790927431938.png" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/main-fistula-scaled-e1790927431938.png" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/main-fistula-scaled-e1790927431938.png&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
KARACHI, Pakistan, October 2 (IPS)  - “You’re living a life drained of joy,” is how Shehnaz Sher Ali describes her “perpetually wet and stinky” existence. “I wouldn’t wish it on my worst enemy,” says the 35-year-old, who travelled by bus for more than 12 hours with her husband from their village in Rahim Yar Khan, Punjab, changing diapers whenever possible to keep the smell from reaching the fellow passengers.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44241&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “For Pakistan Rising Fistula Cases Make SDG 3 Goal Elusive”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44240</id><title>SUDAN: ‘It’s Shocking to Be Forced into Silence Simply Because You Are a Refugee’</title><updated>2026-10-02T07:32:45-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44240" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/anonymous_021026-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;CIVICUS discusses life as a refugee with an exiled Sudanese civil society activist who has asked to remain anonymous for security reasons.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44240&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “SUDAN: ‘It’s Shocking to Be Forced into Silence Simply Because You Are a Refugee’”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44239</id><title>The Ingenuity Trap</title><updated>2026-10-02T05:54:48-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44239" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Mariam-Daher_.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Mariam-Daher_.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Mariam-Daher_-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/10/Mariam-Daher_.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
DOHA, Qatar, October 2 (IPS)  - In the 21st century, getting a pencil into Gaza became international news. In January, after more than two years of restrictions, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.rte.ie/news/middle-east/2026/0127/1555329-gaza-israel/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;UNICEF finally brought in learning kits with pencils and exercise books&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/9/20/back-to-school-in-gaza-learning-in-tents-after-years-of-disruption&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Textbooks stayed out&lt;/a&gt;. By then, the UN had recorded damage to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.un.org/unispal/document/unicef-humanitarian-action-appeal-for-children-2026-state-of-palestine-revision-1-february-2026/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;97.5 per cent of Gaza’s schools&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44239&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “The Ingenuity Trap”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44238</id><title>If We Can Start an Epoch, We Can Start a Farming Revolution</title><updated>2026-10-02T05:01:32-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44238" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Members-of-Smallholder_01.jpg" /><media:content url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Members-of-Smallholder_01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Members-of-Smallholder_01-100x100.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://static.globalissues.org/ips/2026/09/Members-of-Smallholder_01.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;
NEW YORK, October 2 (IPS)  - In November 1952, the United States detonated the world’s first thermonuclear device at Enewetak Atoll in the Marshall Islands. The test, code-named Ivy Mike, erased the island of Elugelab and scattered a signature of plutonium across the planet that remains in lake beds, ice sheets and ocean sediments today.
&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44238&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “If We Can Start an Epoch, We Can Start a Farming Revolution”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44250</id><title>‘Money alone won’t get us there’: UN steps up aid for 12 forgotten crises</title><updated>2026-10-02T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44250" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/13-05-2024-OCHA-Afghanistan.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/13-05-2024-OCHA-Afghanistan.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/13-05-2024-OCHA-Afghanistan.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/13-05-2024-OCHA-Afghanistan.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Getting aid to people in the world’s most neglected emergencies takes more than money. It takes open roads, open borders and leaders willing to help it reach those in dire need.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44250&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “‘Money alone won’t get us there’: UN steps up aid for 12 forgotten crises”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44249</id><title>Global life expectancy bounces back to near pre-pandemic levels, WHO says</title><updated>2026-10-02T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44249" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/26-09-2022_ADB_India.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/26-09-2022_ADB_India.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/26-09-2022_ADB_India.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Libraries/Production%20Library/26-09-2022_ADB_India.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;People around the world are living longer again, with global life expectancy almost fully recovered from the disruption of the COVID-19 pandemic, the World Health Organization (WHO) said on Friday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44249&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Global life expectancy bounces back to near pre-pandemic levels, WHO says”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44248</id><title>Ukraine war ‘a human rights catastrophe’ that must end, says Türk</title><updated>2026-10-02T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44248" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/02-10-2026-UNOCHA-Ukraine-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/02-10-2026-UNOCHA-Ukraine-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/02-10-2026-UNOCHA-Ukraine-01.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Embargoed/2026/10/02-10-2026-UNOCHA-Ukraine-01.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The war in Ukraine is a human rights catastrophe that is “growing and intensifying by the week” and threatening an even greater disaster across the region, UN High Commissioner for Human Rights Volker Türk said on Friday.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44248&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Ukraine war ‘a human rights catastrophe’ that must end, says Türk”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry><entry><id>https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44247</id><title>Collective action needed to tackle global information crisis, UN-led dialogue hears</title><updated>2026-10-02T05:00:00-07:00</updated><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44247" /><link rel="enclosure" type="image/jpeg" href="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/02-10-2026-UN-Charlotte-Scaddan.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" /><media:content url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/02-10-2026-UN-Charlotte-Scaddan.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg" type="image/jpeg" medium="image" /><media:thumbnail url="https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/02-10-2026-UN-Charlotte-Scaddan.jpg/image100x100cropped.jpg" width="100" height="100" /><summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://global.unitednations.entermediadb.net/assets/mediadb/services/module/asset/downloads/preset/Collections/Production%20Library/2026/10/02-10-2026-UN-Charlotte-Scaddan.jpg/image1170x530cropped.jpg&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Governments, UN entities, civil society, media, academia and the private sector have called for stronger cooperation and practical action to respond to a rapidly changing global information landscape.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globalissues.org/news/2026/10/02/44247&quot;&gt;Read the full story, “Collective action needed to tackle global information crisis, UN-led dialogue hears”, on globalissues.org&lt;/a&gt; →&lt;/p&gt;</summary></entry></feed><!-- 0.0006s ch:1 -->